            <td>Up to 54 TB LPDDR5X</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Networking</td>
            <td>32.4 TB/s</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Inlet temperature</td>
            <td>45°C</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>On NVIDIA's product page, the inference figures are sparse, and the training, FP16, BF16, and TF32 figures are dense. The networking bandwidth counts traffic in both directions. Olympus is NVIDIA's own CPU core design. NVLink-C2C is the link between each Vera CPU and its GPUs. LPDDR5X is a low-power type of memory used by the CPUs. Inlet temperature is how warm the cooling liquid can be when it enters the rack.</p>

